<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <div :if={@question} class="question-page">
    <.link navigate={~p"/"} class="back-link"><.icon name="hero-arrow-left" class="size-4" />
    All questions</.link>
    <div class="question-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">{@question.category}</span><h1 id="question-title">
        {@question.text}
      </h1><p>{@question.description}</p><div class="question-meta">
        <span class="sample-label">SAMPLE DATA</span><span>{@question.total} fictional responses</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="preview-notice" class="preview-notice">
      <.icon name="hero-beaker" class="size-4 shrink-0" /><p>
        This is an example, with synthetic counts. These percentages describe no real sample or population.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="question-detail-grid">
      <section id="results" class="results-panel" aria-labelledby="results-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="results-title">The answer breakdown</h2><a
            id="results-permalink"
            href={(~p"/questions/#{@question.slug}" <> "#results")}
            aria-label="Link to these results"
          ><.icon name="hero-link" class="size-5" /></a>
        </div>
        <div
          :for={{answer, index} <- Enum.with_index(@question.answers)}
          id={"answer-#{index}"}
          class="answer-row"
        >
          <div><span>{answer.label}</span><strong>{answer.percentage}%</strong></div><div class="answer-track">
            <div
              class={"answer-fill answer-color-#{index}"}
              style={"width: #{answer.percentage}%"}
            >
            </div>
          </div><p>{answer.count} example responses</p>
        </div>
        <p class="results-footnote">Unweighted · Synthetic example · Not a population estimate</p>
      </section>
      <aside class="context-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">A NUMBER ISN’T THE WHOLE STORY</span><h2>
          Who answered<br />matters.
        </h2><p>A percentage can describe a sample without representing the wider world.</p><p>
          Look for the source, the wording, and how people were invited to take part.
        </p><a href="#methodology" class="text-link">Read the context
        <.icon name="hero-arrow-down" class="size-4" /></a><.vue
          id="share-question"
          v-component="ShareQuestion"
          v-socket={@socket}
          v-ssr={false}
          path={(~p"/questions/#{@question.slug}" <> "#results")}
        />
      </aside>
    </div>
    <section id="methodology" class="methodology-panel">
      <span class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE NUMBERS</span><h2>Every percentage needs context.</h2><p>
        These results are <strong>synthetic examples</strong>
        created to explore Roughly’s interface. There is no collection period, sampling frame, or real respondent data behind them.
      </p><p>
        When real responses are available, an open poll will tell us about the people who answered. It won’t automatically represent everyone. Sample selection, question wording, and response bias all matter.
      </p><div class="methodology-facts">
        <div><span>SOURCE</span><strong>Interface sample</strong></div><div>
          <span>REPRESENTATIVENESS</span><strong>Not applicable</strong>
        </div><div><span>RESPONSE COLLECTION</span><strong>Not yet open</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="share-note">
      <.icon name="hero-link" class="size-5" /><p>
        A question worth sharing?
        <a class="text-link" href={(~p"/questions/#{@question.slug}" <> "#results")}>Link directly to the results</a>
        from a conversation or article. Include the sample context.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section :if={!@question} id="question-not-found" class="empty-results">
    <h1>We couldn’t find that question.</h1><p>There are more questions to explore.</p><.link
      navigate={~p"/"}
      class="text-link"
    >Back to all questions</.link>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
